  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-EC_INTPA" secondary-reporter="0" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Commission - Directorate-General for International Partnerships</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation of the Graduate Training Program through development and delivery of industry relevant Initial Professional Development (IPD) training</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the Graduate Training Programme (GTP) is to equip unemployed graduates and engage them in the transport sector with the practical skillsets necessary to succeed at the workplace through mentorships as part of the Initial Professional Development. This should start the process of fulfilling the requirements for registering engineers with the Uganda Institution of Professional Engineers (UIPE) and then with the Engineers Registration Board (ERB) as registered engineering professionals. This shall have the effect of improving overall influence and relevance of UIPE to its members and strengthen the institution. This action shall focus on the implementation of the Graduate Training Program that focuses on unemployed graduates under categories E, T1 and T2 representing Engineers, and Technicians from Universities, Training Colleges and Tertiary institutions respectively by providing them with a salary subvention and placement with various employers in the transport industry, coupled with initial professional development which shall be delivered through a Professional Development Manager.</narrative>
  </description>
